From fbd91dcc29a10cfc9898f868c3c6995ca29571ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:22:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] gate -> Q8_1: read the attention gate view in place;
 compute the GDN output norm in the kernel

Two launches fewer per layer on the decode / verify band, both bit-identical:
- Attention output gate: CONT(gate half of each Q head) -> SIGMOID -> MUL ->
  matmul.  The gate -> Q8_1 kernel already takes row strides, so it reads the
  row-strided view directly and the CONT launches nothing (it is an exact copy).
  GGML_CUDA_FUSE_CONT_GATE_Q8_1=0 turns it off.
- GDN output: RMS_NORM(xn) * w is skipped at its node and computed by the gate
  kernel (unary_gated_q8_1_norm_kernel), one 128-wide row per 256-thread block
  exactly as rms_norm_f32<256, true> runs it.  Both nodes take the decision from
  the same predicate (ggml_cuda_gdn_norm_gate_match).  The context records the
  skipped norm and its gate node; the attention-gate fusion leaves a pending
  norm alone, and a skip whose gate node is passed or never reached aborts.
  The match also checks that no node in between writes over the norm's input
  or weight.  GGML_CUDA_FUSE_GDN_NORM_GATE=0 turns it off.

(A two-rows-per-block version of the norm kernel was 1 ulp off in some rows.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
